# Method and Apparatus for Managing Communications of a Moving Platform

A method and apparatus are disclosed for managing communications on a moving platform. The platform comprises a plurality of platform applications, a communications system configured to transmit data received from at least one platform application via wireless communication using one of several supported communication links, and a data management module. The apparatus and method are configured to:

- Receive performance data indicative of the current available bandwidth for each communications link allocated to, or associated with, the platform applications;

- Identify, for each platform application, the data to be transmitted to a recipient node, and compare the bandwidth requirement of that data against the current available bandwidth of the corresponding communications link;

- In instances where this comparison reveals that the current available bandwidth of a communications link is insufficient to meet the bandwidth requirement of a given platform application, generate information data and transmit it to the specified platform application, or to its associated quality of service interface; and

- Upon receipt of the information data, enable the specified platform application, or its associated quality of service interface, to adapt at least one parameter of its application data to align with the current available bandwidth of the corresponding communications link, thereby facilitating transmission to the recipient node.

